Dear Marco,

Here is what you want. You just needed to add the grouping when your x (or y) variable is a factor. Please check the rest of the code. Note that I don't use attach() and detach(). That's a disaster waiting to happen. Use the names of the data.frame instead or use something like with() or within().

newfood1 <- read.table("http://dl.dropbox.com/u/51420824/newfood1.txt", header = TRUE)

library(reshape)
df.new <http://df.new> <- melt(newfood1, id.vars = "Individual", variable_name = "Time")
df.new <http://df.new>$Weight <- df.new <http://df.new>$value

with(df.new <http://df.new>, interaction.plot(Time, Individual, Weight, ylab = "Body weight (g)", xlab = "Time", main="Change in the body weight of bats after being given a new food", col = rainbow(10)))
library(ggplot2)
df.new <http://df.new>$Individual <- factor(df.new <http://df.new>$Individual)
ggplot(df.new <http://df.new>, aes(Time, Weight, colour = Individual, linetype = Individual, group = Individual)) + geom_line()

Best regards,

Thierry

