Hi there,

I am having some trouble with a graph and hope somebody is willing to
lend some expertise.

I have a large dataset of daily historic water elevation levels from a
reservoir (from 60's to present), and regularly produce ggplot graphs
to show recent daily reservoir elevations in contrast to historic
elevations.  I prefer to plot the recent reservoir elevations against
boxplots of the historic reservoir elevations, which gives the reader
an easy reference of how the annual elevations compared with historic
elevations.

My method has been to give all dates a fake date with a common year
(2011), so that daily values can be compiled for each day of the year,
and then create boxplots using the group argument to bin the data by
week. I then plot the recent daily values using geom_line from a new
secondary dataframe - a subset of the full dataset (I call this
dataset 'overlay').

My problem is that I would like to plot mulitiple lines, each from
different periods of time (e.g., elevations from several different
years) overtop of the historic boxplots (no problem, except that); I
also want each line to be plotted with a different colour to indicate
the year (this is what I cannot do).

Is there a way of defining colour for my 'overlay' data set? or is
there a better approach that I have overlooked?

I have provided some mock-up data, and an example of how I am plotting
three lines, one for each year, over top of the boxplots summarizing
all years.

MANY thanks in advance.

Here is my code:

#generate some date data
#(May to August, 2008 to 2010:

day <- c(1:30)
month <- c(rep(5,30), rep(6,30), rep(7,30), rep(8,30))
year <- c(rep(2008,120),rep(2009,120),rep(2010,120))
df <- data.frame(year, month, day)
yr <- 2011
df$date <- as.Date(paste(yr,month,day,sep="-"))
#notice that 2011 is entered
# as the year so that the
# data can be superimposed

#generate some water elevation data,
# with different mean each year:

df$elev <- runif(360,435,440)
df$elev <- ifelse(df$year==2008,df$elev-5,df$elev)
df$elev <- ifelse(df$year==2009,df$elev-10,df$elev)

p <- ggplot(df,aes(date, elev, group = floor_date(date, "1 week")))
p <- p + geom_boxplot(outlier.size = 2, outlier.colour = "darkgrey",
outlier.shape = 1)
p <- p + scale_x_date(format = "%b")
p <- p + labs(x = "Date", y = "Reservoir Elevation (m)")

p

for (i in c("2008","2009","2010")){

overlay <- df[which(df$year==i),]
p <- p + geom_line(data = overlay, colour = "red", size = 1)

}

p

