On Wed, Dec 14, 2011 at 10:52 AM, Winston Chang <winsto...@gmail.com> wrote:
> On Wed, Dec 14, 2011 at 12:19 PM, Harry van Oort <hvan...@gmail.com> wrote:
> > But in the graph you provide, the boxplot only maps the 2010 data.... doesn't it?
> >
> > The boxplots needs to display ALL years of data, while the differently coloured lines should only be drawn for a subset of the years. Thats the problem.
>
>
> I have two possible solutions for you, if I understand the problem correctly.
>
> # Set up the data
> day <- c(1:30)
> month <- c(rep(5,30), rep(6,30), rep(7,30), rep(8,30))
> year <- c(rep(2008,120),rep(2009,120),rep(2010,120))
> df <- data.frame(year, month, day)
> yr <- 2011
> df$date <- as.Date(paste(yr,month,day,sep="-"))
> df$elev <- runif(360,435,440)
> df$elev <- ifelse(df$year==2008,df$elev-5,df$elev)
> df$elev <- ifelse(df$year==2009,df$elev-10,df$elev)
>
> # First version
> p <- ggplot(df,aes(date, elev, group = floor_date(date, "1 week"))) +
>   geom_boxplot(outlier.size = 2, outlier.colour = "darkgrey",
>                outlier.shape = 1) +
>   scale_x_date(format = "%b") +
>   labs(x = "Date", y = "Reservoir Elevation (m)") +
>   geom_line(data = subset(df, year=="2009"), aes(colour = "2009"), size = 1) +
>   geom_line(data = subset(df, year=="2010"), aes(colour = "2010"), size = 1)
> p
>
> # Second version
> p1 <- ggplot(df,aes(date, elev, group = floor_date(date, "1 week"))) +
>   geom_boxplot(outlier.size = 2, outlier.colour = "darkgrey",
>                outlier.shape = 1) +
>   scale_x_date(format = "%b") +
>   labs(x = "Date", y = "Reservoir Elevation (m)") +
>   geom_line(data = subset(df, year %in% c("2009", "2010")), size=1,
>             aes(colour = as.factor(year),
>                 group = interaction(year, floor_date(date, "1 week"))))
> p1
>
>
>
> In the first one, you manually add each set of lines for each year. I couldn't get it to work in a loop with "aes(colour=i)" because of the way that ggplot escapes and evaluates variable names in aes specifications. Maybe someone who understands that stuff better can figure it out.
>
> In the second one, the group specification is very important. It says that each combination of year and week is one group, and so a separate line will be drawn for each group. The year also has to be treated as a factor rather than as a continuous variable.
>
> -Winston

